c(1, "header lines 1-7; §2.1; §2.1 table (verbatim); §2.2 table (verbatim)", "positioning", "Roubit : Fun Routine Planner (App Store ID 1527382961, com.roubit) by Roubit Inc. ((주)루빗, Korea), released 2020-11-05, current 6.5.9 (2026-09-08), KR name '루빗 - 귀여운 습관 할일 투두 계획 자기계발 루틴', English and Korean only, 'Contains Advertising', 9+ with 'Health or Wellness Topics' — a routine and to-do app built around a baby bunny that grows as you complete routines; routines earn carrots → coins, fragments and gems spent on furniture, themes and outfits partly through a gacha; a diary with mood logging, an AI 'support letter' replying to diary entries (from April 2023), Dr. Eddy an AI counsellor chat (2023-08 → 2024-10), daily quotes and fortune cookies, statistics, alarms that repeat until done, NFC tag check-ins (Korea), widgets, invite codes, and from January 2026 a friend feature. Feature inventory (verbatim): " + table("## 2.1 What the product is", 0) + " || listing (verbatim): " + table("## 2.2 What the store listing says", 0), "free with 8-routine cap, ads, gacha; monthly $7.49 / ₩6,600, yearly $59.99 / ₩55,000; consumable Gold Carrots", "praise", "500 reviews, 40 storefronts, 14 languages, 2020-11-14 → 2026-09-01 (2,118 days), mean 4.156★; KR 246, US 61, JP 56; 112 codes; 2,007 assignments", "none", "header", "app-specific", ["11575242405", "8290633106", "9866716493"], "", "half the corpus is Korean")

c(2, "How to read this; Nine warnings 2, 3, 4, 6, 7; §1.1 table (verbatim); §1.2 table (verbatim); §1.3 table (verbatim); §1.4; §1.5 table (verbatim); §1.6", "data-caveat", "Method and limits: every one of 500 reviews read in date order in the original language (ko 251, en 121, ja 55, pt 26, es 22, tr/fr/zh 5 each, de 3, five singletons, two emoji-only), 112 codes in 13 families (108 hand, 4 mechanical), 22 unions, 2,007 assignments, 85 checks (first run caught 27 real errors), 24 absence tests; no duplicates, no repeat authors, 22 edited; three eligible storefronts (KR 246, US 61, JP 56 = 72.60%), 17 storefronts with one review; no version field and release notes only from 2025-09-16 — every release link is timing, not cause; 145 reviews (29.00%) under 60 characters; only 31 carry helpful votes (17 in Japan); PAID_EXPLICIT 27 (5.40%) is not a conversion rate; the app and its AI features were not tested. Bands (verbatim): " + table("## 1.5 Signal thresholds", 0) + " — at n=500 one review is 0.20%; in the US 1.6%, Japan 1.8%.", "n/a", "mixed", "500/500 read; 112 codes; 85 checks; 24 absence tests; low-info 145 (29.00%)", "none", "method", "generalisable", ["11575242405"], "", "")

c(3, "Warning 1; §1.6 #1; §6.8", "data-caveat", "These reviewers are not a negatively selected minority: 3,320 public ratings across the same 40 storefronts average 4.658★ vs the corpus 4.156★ — a gap of only +0.502★, small in Korea (4.71 vs 4.37) and the US (4.72 vs 4.20), large in Japan (4.48 vs 3.36); 'most text reviews here are written by people who like the app'.", "n/a", "mixed", "gap +0.502★; KR +0.34; US +0.52; JP +1.12", "none", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["11575242405"], "", "")

c(4, "§0.1; §0.1 table (verbatim); §3.2", "insight", "The bunny, the room and the letters are what people pay attention to: U:praise_any 369 (73.80%, CI 69.8–77.5%, 4.60★), U:praise_specific 284 (56.80%) (verbatim): " + table("## 0.1 The bunny", 0) + " — 'the game loop gets people to open the app, and opening it gets the routine done': '방꾸미려고 앱 들어가서 자동으로 할일까지 다 하는느낌' (I go in to decorate the room and end up doing all my tasks automatically, 5★); a reviewer installed five highly rated apps and 'the only one that survived was Roubit'; a Japanese 3★ uninstalling still calls 'habit app × gacha game' an excellent idea; the support letter is the feature singled out most since launch (2023-04-27) — 21.7% of E3 reviews; 'the diary replies are better than talking with my friends' (br 5★).", "free gamified loop + AI letter", "praise", "praise_any 369 / 73.80% / 4.60★; character_game 192 (38.40%); CUTE 157 (31.40%); OUT_HABIT_BUILT 97 (19.40%); GAMIFICATION 76 (15.20%); letter_ai_praise 74 (14.80%); EMOTIONAL_SUPPORT 64 (12.80%)", "build-free", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["11575242405", "8290633106", "13956187658", "9866716493", "12161555324"], "", "")

c(5, "§0.2; §7.3; §8.1", "must-never-break", "In two waves the Diary and Settings tabs stopped opening: BUG_DIARY_SETTINGS_BLANK 40 (8.00%, CI 5.9–10.7%) — first 2025-11-06, last 2026-06-09, none before; wave 1: 14 of 15 reviews posted 2025-11-06 → 11-10 (KR 6, JP 8); wave 2: 26 of 37 posted 2026-05-16 → 06-09 (36 of 37 report some defect); Settings holds the support form and account deletion, so the bug cut off the way to report it (SUPPORT_UNREACHABLE_INAPP 6: '設定にもいけないから不具合報告が出来なくてやむなくこちらに書かせて頂きました'); the diary holds years of personal writing (DATA_LOSS 11: '제 2년의 추억이 모두 들어가있는 앱 입니다'; 'I'd at least like to see the diary I wrote for a year, but I can't'); loyal users filed these, 19 of 40 at four or five stars ('70렙찍고 이렇게 됬는데 제발 제 최애 인생 루틴앱인데 고쳐주시면 감사하겠습니다' — level 70 after 18 months); the 6.4.52 note (2026-06-09) 'If the diary list cannot be loaded, a helpful message is shown instead of a blank screen'; reports stop after it but with 11 reviews since 'the stop is weak evidence of a fix'.", "diary/settings tab blank after releases", "1★-burst", "BUG_DIARY_SETTINGS_BLANK 40 / 8.00%; wave 1 14/15; wave 2 26/37; 19 of 40 4–5★; DATA_LOSS 11; SUPPORT_UNREACHABLE_INAPP 6", "must-never-break", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["13372186913", "14123175914", "13370906696", "14093228593", "14074890592"], "a bug in the settings tab removes the support form and the account-deletion path with it", "")

c(6, "§0.3; §3.11; §8.3; Warning 9", "audience", "For a meaningful minority this is a mental-health tool: U:mental_health_any 68 (13.60%, CI 10.9–16.9%, mean 4.84★); USE_MENTAL_HEALTH 16 (3.20%) name depression, anxiety, ADHD, autism, a crisis or suicidal thoughts — '몇년간 우울증에 허덕이는 저를 조금이라도 움직일수 있게 해주는 앱이에요' (an app that gets me, who has struggled with depression for years, to move even a little); 'I am autistic and find it very hard to manage routines'; two safety-relevant reviews — '제가 죽고싶었을때가 있는데 이거 덕분에 지금 제가 여기있었어요' (there was a time I wanted to die; thanks to this I'm here now); 'No es una exageración decir que esta aplicación me salvó la vida'; one notes the letters point to professional help ('sempre indicando a procura por um profissional'); 'the letter feature is receiving crisis-level disclosures. How it handles them is a product-safety question, not only a delight feature.'", "AI letter replies to diary incl. crisis content", "praise", "mental_health_any 68 / 13.60% / 4.84★; USE_MENTAL_HEALTH 16; crisis disclosures 2", "must-have", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["10866655553", "13303553647", "12738770364", "13873857942", "13429711572"], "", "")

c(7, "§0.4; §3.5; §8.2", "must-never-break", "Many people never got in: U:cant_use_app 88 (17.60%, CI 14.5–21.2%, mean 3.23★) — blank Diary/Settings 40, BUG_LAUNCH_LOAD 26 (5.20%), BUG_LOGIN_SIGNUP 16 (3.20%), BUG_CRASH 11 (2.20%), BUG_UPDATE_LOOP 7 (1.40%); in the US the problem is getting in at all — BUG_LAUNCH_LOAD 7 of 61 (11.5%) vs 4.3% elsewhere ('i have never been able to use it because it does not load'; 'it just infinitely loads. Unusable.'); U:defect_any 180 (36.00%); 46 of the 62 one- and two-star reviews describe a defect or being blocked.", "launch/login failures, esp. US", "1★-burst", "cant_use_app 88 / 17.60% / 3.23★; LAUNCH_LOAD 26; LOGIN_SIGNUP 16; CRASH 11; UPDATE_LOOP 7; defect_any 180 / 36.00%; US launch 11.5%", "must-never-break", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["14320708889", "13156744094"], "", "")

c(8, "§0.5; §3.6; §8.5", "monetization", "Monetisation friction is mild; price and the lack of a one-time option are the Korean objections: U:paywall_friction 61 (12.20%, mean 3.85★) spread thinly — FREE_LIMIT_ROUTINES 12 (2.40%), ADS_IN_APP 12, PRICE_TOO_HIGH 10 (2.00%), PAYWALL_LETTERS_AI 8, PRICE_OPAQUE 8, WANT_ONE_TIME_PURCHASE 6 (1.20%); the free tier is praised more than attacked (PRAISE_FREE_GENEROUS 14: 'literally gives you supportive letters every day FOR FREE'); Korea: '동물의숲이 평생에 5만원인데 루틴 앱이 1년에 5만5천원… 결제를 못하겠어서 속상한 앱은 처음이에요' (Animal Crossing is ₩50,000 for life; a routine app is ₩55,000 a year… the first app where I'm upset that I can't bring myself to pay, 5★); WOULD_PAY_INTENT 11 of 246 in Korea vs 1 of 254 elsewhere; PAID_EXPLICIT 27 (5.40%), 12 satisfied, 14 report a defect.", "yearly ₩55,000 / $59.99; no lifetime", "mixed", "paywall_friction 61 / 12.20% / 3.85★; PRICE_TOO_HIGH 10; WANT_ONE_TIME 6; PRAISE_FREE_GENEROUS 14; WOULD_PAY KR 11/246", "research", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["14479724385", "11959502740"], "", "Korean users anchor a routine-app subscription against a one-time game")

c(9, "§0.6; §3.6; §8.4", "anti-pattern", "Ads are moving into the core loop: U:ads_any 16 (3.20%) — ADS_IN_APP 12, ADS_FOR_PAST_CHECK 4 (checking off yesterday's routine requires watching an ad: '전 날 놓친 기록 체크하려면 기록 하나 하나 광고를 봐야 체크할 수 있게 해놓은 건 굉장히 많이 불편하네요', 2022, 5★); in 2026 ads cost long-time users — 'アプリを開く時も日記を書く時も広告が流れるようになりました' (ads now play when opening the app and writing the diary, jp 1★); a user of several years: '갑자기 광고가 생기더니 광고 다 봐도 루빗에 아예 접속이 안되네요' (ads suddenly appeared, and even after watching them I can't get in, 1★); a Japanese 3★ uninstalled after a month in which the past-day ad would not load so past tasks could not be completed; release notes 2026-04-29 'watch ads and earn additional rewards', 2026-06-09 'Premium users can now receive rewards without waiting for ads'.", "ads on open, on diary write, and gating past-day check-off", "churn", "ads_any 16 / 3.20%; ADS_FOR_PAST_CHECK 4; 2026 ad-driven 1★ 2", "dont", "Very strong", "generalisable", ["8330938138", "13877341723", "14149256600", "13956187658"], "an ad that fails to load blocks the recovery action it gates", "")

c(10, "§0.7; §3.8; §8.7", "market", "The app spread internationally before it spoke other languages: English speakers arrived in 2022 through Twitter to a Korean-only app — LANG_REQUEST 11 (2.20%), 7 of 38 (18.4%) E2 reviews ('i downloaded it and tried my best to translate each part but its tiring'; 'in developer the language said it was on korean and english but inside the app you can only use korean'); Korean text still appears in 2026 — LOCALIZATION_INCOMPLETE 5 ('ハングルで読めない' — the gacha; 'me aparecen letras coreanas' — the store tab); requests for Chinese (3) and Vietnamese (1) remain open; the listing supports English and Korean only.", "EN + KO only; partial", "complaint", "LANG_REQUEST 11 / 2.20%, E2 18.4%; LOCALIZATION_INCOMPLETE 5", "do", "Meaningful", "generalisable", ["9049739687", "9047952818", "14090994337", "14017493057", "11397949222", "11042639191"], "", "")

c(11, "§0.8; §3.10; §4.7", "data-caveat", "Reviews are being used as a support desk: SUPPORT_QUESTION 43 (8.60%); META_RATING_TEXT_MISMATCH 33 (6.60%) — 31 of 33 are four- or five-star reviews containing only a complaint or question, 27 of them a defect; U:support_negative 15 (3.00%, 2.53★): unanswered email ('担当者の方へメールも2度しましたが、返信もなく'), unread KakaoTalk messages, a promised same-day fix followed by three days of silence; support that worked changed the rating — a Turkish reviewer moved to five stars ('The support helped me fix the ad issue by using the Restore Subscription button'); 'the only issue / bug I've had was sorted within 24 hours'.", "support form inside the (broken) Settings tab; email; KakaoTalk", "mixed", "SUPPORT_QUESTION 43 / 8.60%; MISMATCH 33 (31 high-star); support_negative 15 / 2.53★", "must-have", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["14138599777", "14142547272", "13852438902", "13812322981", "13303553647"], "", "")

c(12, "§0.9; §2.4; §2.5", "data-caveat", "Absent: no Family Sharing mention, no Android comparison, no data-export or backup request, no battery complaint (one overheating report), one tracking objection ('the app tracks you', 5★); Apple Watch or iPad requested only from Korea (REQ_IPAD_WATCH_MAC 15, all KR); refunds mentioned twice. Privacy: label 'Data Not Linked to You' incl. advertising and analytics uses and precise location; 'the diary contains mental-health and crisis disclosures that are sent to an AI to generate letters; no review asks where that text goes'. Not establishable: downloads/conversion/churn, release history before 2025-09, what the AI does with crisis content, whether Dr. Eddy still exists, historical prices, why the diary tab blanked.", "n/a", "mixed", "24 absence tests; PRIV objection 1; REQ_IPAD_WATCH_MAC 15 (KR)", "research", "absence test", "generalisable", ["11213578473", "13473580389"], "", "")

c(13, "§2.3 table (verbatim); §2.3", "monetization", "Free / paid / trial / unclear (verbatim): " + table("## 2.3 Free / paid / trial", 0) + " — the routine cap moved 150 records (2021) → 8 (most) → 9 (2023-02) → 4 (2025-02); letters limited free (2 replies / 2 a week / 'second day you have to pay' / ads to unlock), unlimited on the KR yearly plan; Ultimate themes and outfits paid; no ads paid ('about $60/yr'); past-day check-off ad-gated; NFC forced tag on the monthly plan with stickers sold separately; 7-day trial then billing.", "free: cap, diary, bunny, room; paid: unlimited routines, unlimited letters (yearly), Ultimate cosmetics, no ads, NFC; consumables", "mixed", "FREE_LIMIT_ROUTINES 12; PAYWALL_LETTERS_AI 8; PAYWALL_COSMETICS 4; TRIAL_USER 4; prices ₩39,000 (2023) → ₩55,000 (2024–); $7.99; ¥6,000", "undecided", "table", "app-specific", ["11019712270", "11117435473", "12290405993", "14161345933", "12165498115", "12509850218", "10580947058", "10783100144"], "", "")

